wolves and glittery vampires unite for a  look back at the final days on the set  of twilight every film has been like a  family reunion in the years since the  record-breaking blockbuster franchise  came to a close the cast have revealed a  ton about the very end of production  from breakdowns of the stars last days  and parting gifts to their most brutally  honest thoughts on the twilight movies  a lot of stuff in the toilet world that  doesn't make any sense robert pattinson  and kristen stewart's very last scene  was bella and edward's deer hunt in the  woods and since the rest of the cast had  already wrapped robb felt it was  ridiculous to bother getting emotional  with just the two of them  don't say goodbye to anyone kristin  probably wasn't in the mood either since  the very last thing she did on set was  step on a nail the duo's final day on  the twilight franchise was a lot more  anticlimactic than the twyhards were  probably hoping for  taylor lautner left the world of  twilight on a pretty lonely note this is  painful while his second to last day was  spent doing a scene with rob and kristen  his final day was spent filming all by  himself although he was sad to have  finished filming alone lautner still  managed to see the bright side of things  it was a little emotional but i mean the  good news is we will be able to promote  breaking dawn part 1 and 2 together for  the next year and a half  jackson rathbone and ashley greene were  lucky enough to have two last days their  last day with the director bill condon  and the rest of the first unit crew was  the wedding reception with everyone  there including nikki reed whose last  day it actually was that was your last  thing yeah as lovely as that send-off  would have been for them the moment  didn't really sink in for the duo since  they and kellen lutz still had one more  day of fight scenes to film with the  second unit unfortunately the last day  was a little less enjoyable even though  the last day was like 15 16 hours it was  raining and wet and then everybody was  just excited to get home the streak of  anticlimactic last days continues with  co-stars elizabeth reeser and peter  facianelli for their final day filming  on the twilight franchise the heads of  the cullen clan did a simple scene of  them walking up from the backyard of the  cullen house and unlike ashley green and  jackson rathbone the moment sunk in for  them immediately and we just hugged for  like five minutes  and then we went to dinner then we went  to dinner  actor anna kendrick found her experience  on twilight to be both very challenging  and weirdly bonding and she will not  miss it kendrick played a much smaller  role later on in the series which meant  a lot less time on the set for breaking  dawn not only did she not have to show  up until the final day of shooting with  the first unit but she also had to  promote breaking dawn part one i can  tell you this i'm not in breaking dawn  part two so i don't have to talk about  it  i'm just kidding taylor lautner had a  couple of things from twilight that he  was happy to say goodbye to including  taking his shirt off while it may have  been a treat for fans lautner did not  enjoy being the only one who was  shirtless on set especially in the cold  and wet conditions they always filmed in  but for lautner nothing was worse than  having to wear that dreaded wig there  was hatred between both of us it did not  like me i did not like it not fond  memories  after playing esme cullen for a whopping  five movies the only thing actor  elizabeth reeser wishes she had done was  take a memento to commemorate her time  on the twilight franchise i regret that  i didn't steal anything but i found that  stealing from sets is not good she was  not alone as fellow clan member nikki  reed was also too afraid to swipe  anything  i just was feeling so nervous that i  would be in trouble after rapping on the  twilight movies actor nikki reed  revealed some on-set tension between her  and co-stars kristen stewart and robert  pattinson likely stemming from her  alleged love triangle with robert and  kristen and her character's absence from  most of new moon reed felt that the  family dynamic on set had disappeared by  the end i don't feel particularly  sentimental i feel like we're all sort  of ready to graduate middle school and  move on to whatever the next chapter is  but we'll always be this  once his time on twilight was finished  kellen lutz was not afraid to get candid  about the franchise especially when it  came to the writing i didn't like the  script how scary would a glimmering  vampire really be it just doesn't make  sense he was also not a big fan of  shooting days with the entire ensemble  cast griping that he would often just  end up standing around all day with  nothing to do but when it came to his  own character lutz was surprisingly  sentimental there's a lot of emmett in  kellen and a lot of kellen and emmett  and i'm going to bring emmett with me  for the rest of my life  robert pattinson has never been one to  hide his true feelings especially when  it comes to the twilight movies he felt  weird representing a franchise that he  was not a particular fan of and when he  was asked if he would have gone to see  twilight if he wasn't in it his response  was pretty blunt i would just mindlessly  hate it despite his distaste for the  films he did admit he'll miss filming  them just a little yeah i think i will  miss it a bit one thing elizabeth reeser  won't miss is the colored contact lenses  the vampires in the cast were forced to  wear and peter faginelli elaborated on  why i remember elizabeth woke up one day  and her eyes were swollen shut i was  like i play a doctor but i can't help  you elizabeth actor maggie grace chimed  in as well adding that some of the  contacts were even hard to see through  it was funny some you could see through  and some you just couldn't so it was a  little strange to be you know in a scene  with someone that you couldn't see  co-stars kristen stewart robert  pattinson and michael sheen were not  fans of the painful contacts either so  glad to see you here after all the  lovable on-screen couple of ashley green  and jackson rathbone had an equally  lovable view with their time with their  cast members off-screen the two  described every film after the first as  a kind of family reunion and felt that  growing up together on these films  really bonded the core cast however  there were also a number of things they  definitely won't miss about twilight  including the dreary weather white  makeup long night shoots and those  annoying wigs the contacts the wigs the  wigs  for breaking dawn kellen lutz wanted to  add a little more muscle to his already  ripped frame but he may have gone a  little overboard i caught really big  seven months of working out that's  double the time we had for the other  movies i was just eating and working out  because i had a lot of down time so i  just would watch football in the gym  work out so after they wrapped let's  chilled on the workouts for a little  while i think we can all agree kellen  earned himself a break  after his extensive time on twilight  peter facinelli was determined to get  his own unique parting gift carlisle's  ring he had actually been caught trying  to swipe it from the set on the first  movie but with the series coming to an  end he saw another opportunity and  pounced on it when we did breaking dawn  part 2 it might have or it might not  have been left on my finger when i got  home  thanks to the staggered scheduling and  multiple shooting units the final  confrontation in breaking dawn part 2  was the first and last time the entire  cast was together that fact made things  a bit bittersweet for some of the actors  including peter faginelli the other day  when we shot that ending sequence we  knew that was the ending of the last two  movies and it got a little melancholy it  was sad on the bright side for  fatcinelli that specific sequence took  several weeks to film so the cast had  plenty of time to spend together however  robert pattinson wasn't so psyched about  the lengthy shoot being on a piece of  fake snow surrounded by green screen for  like a month it's driving me absolutely  insane  and then they just end it and it's like  well okay well that's that with the  addition of the young mackenzie foy for  the breaking dawn productions the crew  introduced a swear jar to try and keep a  lid on the profanity on set which cast  members do you think contributed the  most to the jar could you keep a lid on  your own salty language let us know in  the comments  you
 

